IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-time`
IMPORT `vmu-s04-s05-values`
IMPORT `vmu-s11-s12-2012-and-sla`

-- Tests of sections 11 and 12.
-- Each expected value is worked out by hand from the quoted line above it.

§ `Section 11 -- Provisions for 2012 to 2013`

-- The rate that section 11(3) gives for 2012 (0.025) fed into the ceiling of section 5(6), for a fee unit of 12 dollars in the previous year.
-- The rate is a proportion, so the ceiling is 12 x (1 + 0.025) = 12.3 dollars.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount section 5(6) compares with for a fee unit of 12 dollars, with the rate section 11(3) gives for 2012` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` 2012 NOTHING NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rate THEN `s 5(6) -- the product, rounded to the nearest cent` 12 rate

#ASSERT `the amount section 5(6) compares with for a fee unit of 12 dollars, with the rate section 11(3) gives for 2012` EQUALS JUST 12.3


-- src:119 | (1) Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012—
-- src:120 | (a) the value of a fee unit is $12.53; and
-- "Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012— (a) the value of a fee unit is $12.53".
-- Arguments in order: the year; the Treasurer fixed an amount by Gazette notice; the amount fixed.
-- In 2012 the value is 12.53 whatever the Treasurer fixed, and whether or not a notice was published.
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2012 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 12.53
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2012 TRUE 99 EQUALS JUST 12.53
-- The year before and the year after are not that year: section 5(1) decides.
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2011 TRUE 12 EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2013 TRUE 12.9 EQUALS JUST 12.9
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2011 FALSE 12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2013 FALSE 12.9 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:121 | (b) the value of a penalty unit is $140.84.
-- "(b) the value of a penalty unit is $140.84."
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2012 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 140.84
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2012 TRUE 999 EQUALS JUST 140.84
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2011 TRUE 130 EQUALS JUST 130
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2013 TRUE 145 EQUALS JUST 145
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2011 FALSE 130 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year, with section 11(2)` 2013 FALSE 145 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:123 | (3) Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%.
-- "Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%."
-- Arguments in order: the year; the annual rate fixed under section 5(4) for the year; the annual rate determined for the previous year.
-- In 2012 the rate is 0.025 whatever was fixed.
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` 2012 NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0.025
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` 2012 (JUST 0.03) (JUST 0.02) EQUALS JUST 0.025
-- 2011 and 2013 follow section 5(5): a rate fixed is the rate; otherwise the previous year's; otherwise none.
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` 2013 (JUST 0.03) (JUST 0.025) EQUALS JUST 0.03
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` 2013 NOTHING (JUST 0.025) EQUALS JUST 0.025
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` 2013 NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` 2011 NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year, with section 11(4)` 2011 (JUST 0.02) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0.02

-- src:119 | (1) Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012—
-- For 2012 the text states the values "Despite sections 5 and 6" and does not say whether notice is still due before 1 June: NOTHING. Other years: the day before 1 June.
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- the last day on which notice of the values may be published, for the financial year` 2012 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- the last day on which notice of the values may be published, for the financial year` 2011 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 5 2011)
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- the last day on which notice of the values may be published, for the financial year` 2013 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 5 2013)

-- src:123 | (3) Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%.
-- For 2012: NOTHING. Other years: the day before 1 March, which in 2011 is 28 February and in 2016 (a leap year) is 29 February.
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the last day on which the annual rate may be fixed, for the financial year` 2012 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the last day on which the annual rate may be fixed, for the financial year` 2011 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2011)
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- the last day on which the annual rate may be fixed, for the financial year` 2016 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2016)

§ `Section 12 -- Subordinate Legislation Act 1994`

-- src:127 | Nothing in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing of—
-- src:128 | (a) a fee or penalty unit in accordance with section 5 or 11; or
-- src:129 | (b) an annual rate in accordance with section 5 or 11.
-- "Nothing in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing of— (a) a fee or penalty unit in accordance with section 5 or 11; or (b) an annual rate in accordance with section 5 or 11."
-- The fixings named, made under section 5 or 11: the Act does not apply (JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` `a fee unit` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` `a penalty unit` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` `an annual rate` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A fixing not made under section 5 or 11, or a fixing of something else: the text says neither yes nor no.
#ASSERT `s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` `a fee unit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` `an annual rate` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` `something else` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12 -- the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing` `something else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
